# Cloudflare Pages custom headers.
#
# @cloudflare/next-on-pages APPENDS its own immutable-asset block to this file at build
# time, between "START/END AUTOGENERATED" markers. Do not add rules inside those markers;
# they are rewritten on every build. Everything here is preserved.

# The agent-readable copies of /lab. Served as text/markdown so a client that content-
# negotiates gets a document rather than an unknown type it decides to download.
# See scripts/build-agent-markdown.mjs for why these live at /md/lab/ and not /lab/*.md.
/md/lab/*
  Content-Type: text/markdown; charset=utf-8
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600

/llms.txt
  Content-Type: text/markdown; charset=utf-8
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600

/llms-full.txt
  Content-Type: text/markdown; charset=utf-8
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600

# ⚠️ Do not add rules here for /lab, /blog or any other page route. **This file only
# affects static assets.** Rules matching a path served by the Pages Function are silently
# ignored — tested: a `Link:` header on /lab/* never appeared on the response, while the
# /md/lab/* rules above applied. Cloudflare's own "Link Headers" diagnostic asks for
# exactly that, and this is the wrong file to satisfy it with.
#
# The working equivalent is `alternates` in the route's generateMetadata, which renders a
# <link rel="alternate"> into the head — see app/lab/[slug]/page.tsx. Real response
# headers on a Function route would need next.config.mjs `headers()`, which is more
# machinery than the signal is worth.
